  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nThe long term forecast remains relatively unchanged. An elongated\neast/west oriented upper level ridge spanning from the northern \nGulf to the northern Baja Peninsula is expected to shift gradually\nto the east into the southern Mississippi Valley by Monday, \nresponding to a large western upper level trough. While the center\nof the ridge will move away from our area, we will still be under\nthe influence of the ridge, keeping our temperatures hot/warmer \nthan normal, and subsidence from the ridge will keep precipitation\nchances out of the forecast for most area. Our far western \ncounties will see a 20% chance for isolated showers and \nthunderstorms at times, but no significant precipitation is \nexpected through the middle of next week. Temperatures will \ncontinue to average from the mid 90s to a few degrees over 100, \nwith lows in the lower 70s to around 80 as well.",
